Shared textures: a texture whose memory another process draws into.

The GPU frame path (ADR 37): rox allocates a texture, lends its memory to a
renderer process as an opaque fd, and samples what the renderer draws into
it with no copy through the CPU. blade 0.7.1 can export and import memory
through `TextureDesc::external`, but the image it makes has a fixed format,
no format list and no external-memory check, and allocation and fd export
`unwrap`, so a driver that says no panics. This adds a module of its own
beside `resource.rs` and leaves that path as it was.

`vulkan/shared.rs`, Vulkan backend on unix only:

- `Context::export_texture(&SharedTextureDesc) -> Result<ExportedTexture,
  SharedTextureError>` makes a 2D image with optimal tiling and a
  dedicated device-local allocation, and exports the memory as an opaque
  fd, with the create info as raw Vulkan values (`SharedImageInfo`) for an
  importer that isn't blade. Before it makes anything it asks
  `vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2` with
  `VkPhysicalDeviceExternalImageFormatInfo` whether this format, usage and
  flag set can be exported as an opaque fd at this size
  (VUID-VkImageCreateInfo-pNext-00990), and says which part failed if not.
- `Context::import_texture(&SharedTextureDesc, OwnedFd, allocation_size,
  memory_type) -> Result<Texture, SharedTextureError>` builds the same
  image, checks the exporter's size and memory type against what this
  device asks of it, and imports. Only test renderers and the Rust example
  renderer call it. rox never imports a renderer's memory: on RADV a lying
  import crashed the importer's process in the driver's own error path.
- `Context::device_identity() -> DeviceIdentity`, the device and driver
  UUIDs an importer compares before it tries, since an opaque fd only means
  something to the same driver on the same device.
- `Context::create_shared_texture_view(Texture, name, TextureFormat,
  TextureUsage) -> Result<TextureView, SharedTextureError>`, a view narrowed
  to the usage given. blade's `create_texture_view` gives a view the
  image's whole usage, and an sRGB view of an image with storage usage
  breaks VUID-VkImageViewCreateInfo-usage-02275.
- `Context::transfer_external_ownership(&mut CommandEncoder, Texture,
  ExternalOwnership)` records the release or the acquire half of an
  ownership transfer to or from `VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL`, in `GENERAL`.

A mutable-format image lists its view formats and then its own format,
which needs Vulkan 1.2 or the call says so. Every failure is a
`SharedTextureError` naming the check or the Vulkan call; nothing on these
paths unwraps on a handle, a size or a driver answer. gpu-alloc asserts on
an out-of-range memory type and on an empty allocation budget, so both are
checked before memory is booked with it.

The module sits inside the Vulkan backend, so the Metal and GLES backends
never compile it, and `cfg(unix)` keeps it off Windows Vulkan builds,
where the handle would not be an fd.

Not a backport. A blade bump re-diffs this against the new source, and a
gpui bump re-checks which blade it pulls in.

